//? Title: Schensted row insertion: actual bumps and paired tableaux
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Insert an integer sequence into rows and retain the insertion tableau P and
recording tableau Q. Native row histories show which value was bumped; the
original permutation [4,1,3,6,2,5] remains the central tableau example.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

In a row, replace the first value strictly greater than the carried value and
carry the replaced value into the next row. If none is greater, append and
record the insertion index in Q. P has weakly increasing rows and strictly
increasing columns; Q has the same shape. For distinct inputs, Schensted's
theorem identifies the first row length with the strict longest increasing
subsequence length. With duplicates, this insertion convention instead
corresponds to a longest nondecreasing subsequence. Direct row scans take O(N^2)
worst-case time and O(N) intrinsic storage.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/schensted_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <numeric>
#include <numbers>
#include <random>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <map>
#include <set>
#include <array>
#include <tuple>
#include <bit>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/schensted.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto r = a::schensted_trace({3, 1, 2});
    std::print("| input index | row | carried | bumped | outgoing (0 on append) | actual row after |\n| " "---: | ---: | ---: | --- | ---: | --- |\n");
    for (const auto &s : r.steps)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | `{}` |\n", s.input_index, s.row,
                   s.carried, s.bumped, s.outgoing, s.after);
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Insert [3,1,2]");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0}, std::format("Actual bumps {}", r.bumps));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("Actual first row {}", r.tableau.p[0]));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/schensted_tiny.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| input index | row | carried | bumped | outgoing (0 on append) | actual row after |
| ---: | ---: | ---: | --- | ---: | --- |
| 0 | 0 | 3 | false | 0 | `[3]` |
| 1 | 0 | 1 | true | 3 | `[1]` |
| 1 | 1 | 3 | false | 0 | `[3]` |
| 2 | 0 | 2 | false | 0 | `[1, 2]` |
\image(figures/schensted_tiny.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Actual small native producing values and decisions; the diagram is generated by the complete program above.)
